==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{from|sh|кошара|t=basket}}, as a direct {{calque|sh|en|basketball|nocap=1}}. Likely 1940s in origin, as earlier news publications use the transcribed term ''basketbal'' (cf. {{m+|de|Basketball}}), sometimes hyphenated, instead.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sh|/kǒʃaːrka/}}
* {{hyphenation|sh|ко|шар|ка}}

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=f|head=ко̀ша̄рка}}

# {{lb|sh|sports}} [[basketball]]

====Usage notes====
The term "basket", similarly to many other European languages, is an informal nickname for basketball, particularly 3-on-3 [[streetball]] games. The official FIBA 3X3 game is often referred to as "basket" by local media, due to its' association with streetball.

